// Pull request: #6540 Sigma: PavinLoader fake-driver MSI campaign (MSBuild from %LOCALAPPDATA%, MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS, fake dllhost/taskhostw tasks, m
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6540
// Pull request author: fotedev
// Change: new rule
// Title: msiexec.exe Spawning cmd.exe to Start an LNK File
// Sigma ID: 9ab49353-da82-4a4e-94e9-603cac795f9e
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: fotedev
// Date: 2026-10-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.003, T1218.007
// Description: Detects msiexec.exe spawning cmd.exe with the pattern "/d /s /c" plus a ".lnk" target. Matches
//   the PavinLoader MSI masquerades (WiX 3.11.1.2318, hidden custom actions SetCA_*/CA_* of type
//   51+242 with MsiHiddenProperties=WixSilentExec64CmdLine) which run: cmd.exe /d /s /c "cd /d <dir>
//   && start "" Antlr3Runtime.lnk" (disguised as Qualcomm Killer Network Service) or
//   MasterDataManager.lnk (disguised as NVIDIA PhysX Runtime). Launching a shortcut from an
//   installer command line this way is uncommon in legitimate MSI packages.
// False positives:
//   - MSI installers that legitimately launch shortcuts through cmd.exe after installation (rare)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/fotedev/pavinloader-easeus-campaign
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1218/007/
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/003/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6ead36c4ad43fd558f6614e9debb235df9de2d40/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_msiexec_spawns_cmd_start_lnk.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\msiexec.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/d /s /c" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".lnk")
